      <Title>Create and review a run plan</Title>
    </DocumentationNarrative>
    <DocumentationNarrative Id="source:cli:meta-orchestration:app:narrative:guide:working-with-metaorchestration" DocumentationSubjectId="source:cli:meta-orchestration:app" PreviousNarrativeId="source:cli:meta-orchestration:app:narrative:summary:summary">
      <Body>`MetaOrchestration` turns pipeline tasks and modeled object access into an executable run graph. It derives dependencies that can be proved from declared reads, writes, and effects, then keeps additional ordering and synchronization as explicit policy.

The orchestration workspace is both the plan and the evidence boundary: it can be inspected before execution and records the result of a run.</Body>
